1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,568
Formulas like distance equals rate times
time are equations with several letters.

2
00:00:06,018 --> 00:00:10,925
In this lesson, we'll rearrange formulas
to solve for whichever letter we need.

3
00:00:12,067 --> 00:00:16,675
An equation with more than one variable is
called a literal equation.

4
00:00:17,125 --> 00:00:21,327
To solve for one letter, treat every other
letter as if it were a number.

5
00:00:21,777 --> 00:00:27,093
Then use the same moves as always: do the
same thing to both sides, and undo

6
00:00:27,093 --> 00:00:29,052
operations in reverse order.

7
00:00:30,200 --> 00:00:32,611
Let's solve d equals r t for t.

8
00:00:33,061 --> 00:00:39,887
t is multiplied by r, so divide both sides
by r. That gives t equals d over r.

9
00:00:40,337 --> 00:00:46,005
Now if you drive a hundred fifty miles at
fifty miles per hour, t equals a hundred

10
00:00:46,005 --> 00:00:48,700
fifty over fifty, which is three hours.

11
00:00:49,833 --> 00:00:56,122
Compare these two equations side by side.
Two x plus three equals eleven, and a x

12
00:00:56,122 --> 00:00:57,364
plus b equals c.

13
00:00:57,814 --> 00:01:04,193
In both, subtract the constant first. Two
x equals eight, and a x equals c minus b.

14
00:01:04,643 --> 00:01:11,363
Then divide by the coefficient. x equals
four, and x equals c minus b, all over a.

15
00:01:11,813 --> 00:01:16,740
The steps are identical. The only
difference is that the answer on the right

16
00:01:16,740 --> 00:01:18,490
is a formula, not a number.

17
00:01:19,633 --> 00:01:26,097
The perimeter of a rectangle is P equals
two l plus two w. Let's solve for w.

18
00:01:26,547 --> 00:01:31,582
Subtract two l from both sides: P minus
two l equals two w.

19
00:01:32,032 --> 00:01:37,365
Divide both sides by two: w equals P minus
two l, all over two.

20
00:01:38,500 --> 00:01:44,279
Here's a famous one. Fahrenheit equals
nine fifths Celsius plus thirty-two. Let's

21
00:01:44,279 --> 00:01:45,135
solve for C.

22
00:01:45,585 --> 00:01:49,958
Subtract thirty-two: F minus thirty-two
equals nine fifths C.

23
00:01:50,408 --> 00:01:56,652
Multiply both sides by five ninths, the
reciprocal of nine fifths. C equals five

24
00:01:56,652 --> 00:02:00,243
ninths, times the quantity F minus
thirty-two.

25
00:02:00,693 --> 00:02:06,391
Check with boiling water. F is two hundred
twelve. Two twelve minus thirty-two is a

26
00:02:06,391 --> 00:02:11,471
hundred eighty, and five ninths of a
hundred eighty is one hundred degrees

27
00:02:11,471 --> 00:02:12,021
Celsius.

28
00:02:13,167 --> 00:02:18,799
Your turn. The area of a triangle is A
equals one half b h. Solve for h.

29
00:02:19,249 --> 00:02:20,785
Pause the video and try it.

30
00:02:21,235 --> 00:02:24,797
Multiply both sides by two: two A equals b
h.

31
00:02:25,247 --> 00:02:28,917
Divide both sides by b: h equals two A
over b.

32
00:02:30,066 --> 00:02:35,357
Ratios, proportions and percents show up
everywhere, from recipes to shopping.

33
00:02:35,807 --> 00:02:40,618
In this lesson, we'll turn them into
equations, and solve them with one simple

34
00:02:40,618 --> 00:02:40,927
tool.

35
00:02:41,066 --> 00:02:47,771
A ratio compares two quantities. If a
class has twelve boys and fifteen girls,

36
00:02:47,771 --> 00:02:51,282
the ratio of boys to girls is twelve to
fifteen.

37
00:02:51,732 --> 00:02:54,399
You can write it with a colon, or as a
fraction.

38
00:02:54,849 --> 00:03:00,412
Like fractions, ratios can be simplified.
Divide both by three, and twelve to

39
00:03:00,412 --> 00:03:02,507
fifteen becomes four to five.

40
00:03:03,633 --> 00:03:09,657
A proportion says two ratios are equal.
For example, x over six equals ten over

41
00:03:09,657 --> 00:03:10,267
fifteen.

42
00:03:10,717 --> 00:03:15,667
To solve it, cross-multiply. Fifteen times
x equals six times ten.

43
00:03:16,117 --> 00:03:21,279
That's fifteen x equals sixty. Divide by
fifteen, and x equals four.

44
00:03:21,729 --> 00:03:27,243
Cross-multiplying works because it's the
same as multiplying both sides by both

45
00:03:27,243 --> 00:03:28,151
denominators.

46
00:03:29,299 --> 00:03:34,481
Here's a real problem. Three notebooks
cost seven dollars fifty. How much do

47
00:03:34,481 --> 00:03:35,913
eight notebooks cost?

48
00:03:36,363 --> 00:03:41,984
Set up matching ratios of notebooks to
dollars: three over seven fifty equals

49
00:03:41,984 --> 00:03:42,933
eight over x.

50
00:03:43,383 --> 00:03:49,720
Cross-multiply: three x equals sixty. So x
equals twenty. Eight notebooks cost twenty

51
00:03:49,720 --> 00:03:50,317
dollars.

52
00:03:51,466 --> 00:03:57,595
A percent is a ratio out of one hundred.
So part over whole equals percent over one

53
00:03:57,595 --> 00:03:58,186
hundred.

54
00:03:58,636 --> 00:04:03,519
What is thirty percent of eighty? Write p
over eighty equals thirty over one

55
00:04:03,519 --> 00:04:04,033
hundred.

56
00:04:04,483 --> 00:04:09,927
Cross-multiply: one hundred p equals two
thousand four hundred. So p equals

57
00:04:09,927 --> 00:04:10,798
twenty-four.

58
00:04:11,248 --> 00:04:16,965
Or, as a shortcut, multiply zero point
three zero by eighty. Same answer.

59
00:04:18,099 --> 00:04:23,081
The same setup finds a missing whole.
Eighteen is forty-five percent of what

60
00:04:23,081 --> 00:04:23,539
number?

61
00:04:23,989 --> 00:04:27,915
Eighteen over w equals forty-five over one
hundred.

62
00:04:28,365 --> 00:04:34,893
Cross-multiply: forty-five w equals one
thousand eight hundred. So w equals forty.

63
00:04:36,033 --> 00:04:39,873
For percent change, divide the change by
the original amount.

64
00:04:40,323 --> 00:04:45,528
A price goes from fifty dollars to sixty
dollars. The change is ten dollars.

65
00:04:45,978 --> 00:04:50,522
Ten over fifty is zero point two, which is
a twenty percent increase.

66
00:04:51,666 --> 00:04:54,397
Your turn. Twelve is what percent of
forty-eight?

67
00:04:54,847 --> 00:04:56,383
Pause the video and try it.

68
00:04:56,833 --> 00:05:00,609
Set up twelve over forty-eight equals p
over one hundred.

69
00:05:01,059 --> 00:05:06,476
Cross-multiply: forty-eight p equals one
thousand two hundred. So p equals

70
00:05:06,476 --> 00:05:10,723
twenty-five. Twelve is twenty-five percent
of forty-eight.

71
00:05:11,866 --> 00:05:14,917
Word problems are where equations become
useful.

72
00:05:15,367 --> 00:05:20,188
In this lesson, we'll turn stories into
equations, using a four-step plan.

73
00:05:21,333 --> 00:05:25,941
Step one: define a variable. Write down
exactly what x stands for.

74
00:05:26,391 --> 00:05:29,271
Step two: translate the words into an
equation.

75
00:05:29,721 --> 00:05:31,534
Step three: solve the equation.

76
00:05:31,984 --> 00:05:36,016
Step four: answer the question in words,
and check that it makes sense.

77
00:05:37,133 --> 00:05:41,506
The sum of three consecutive integers is
seventy-two. What are they?

78
00:05:41,956 --> 00:05:46,735
Let n be the smallest. Then the next two
are n plus one and n plus two.

79
00:05:47,185 --> 00:05:53,253
So n plus n plus one plus n plus two
equals seventy-two. That's three n plus

80
00:05:53,253 --> 00:05:55,249
three equals seventy-two.

81
00:05:55,699 --> 00:06:01,867
Subtract three: three n equals sixty-nine.
So n equals twenty-three. The integers are

82
00:06:01,867 --> 00:06:04,915
twenty-three, twenty-four and twenty-five.

83
00:06:06,033 --> 00:06:11,877
A phone plan costs twenty dollars a month,
plus ten cents per text. One month's bill

84
00:06:11,877 --> 00:06:15,355
was thirty-five dollars. How many texts
were sent?

85
00:06:15,805 --> 00:06:21,864
Let t be the number of texts. Then twenty
plus zero point one t equals thirty-five.

86
00:06:22,314 --> 00:06:28,383
Subtract twenty: zero point one t equals
fifteen. Divide by zero point one: t

87
00:06:28,383 --> 00:06:30,826
equals one hundred fifty texts.

88
00:06:31,966 --> 00:06:37,699
Gym A charges a forty dollar joining fee
plus twenty-five dollars a month. Gym B

89
00:06:37,699 --> 00:06:43,145
charges thirty-five dollars a month with
no fee. When do they cost the same?

90
00:06:43,595 --> 00:06:49,604
Let m be the number of months. Gym A costs
forty plus twenty-five m. Gym B costs

91
00:06:49,604 --> 00:06:50,656
thirty-five m.

92
00:06:51,106 --> 00:06:55,458
Set them equal: forty plus twenty-five m
equals thirty-five m.

93
00:06:55,908 --> 00:07:02,410
Subtract twenty-five m: forty equals ten
m. So m equals four. After four months,

94
00:07:02,410 --> 00:07:05,743
both gyms cost one hundred forty dollars.

95
00:07:05,866 --> 00:07:12,746
A rectangle has a perimeter of fifty-four
centimeters. Its length is three more than

96
00:07:12,746 --> 00:07:15,335
twice its width. Find its dimensions.

97
00:07:15,785 --> 00:07:19,881
Let w be the width. Then the length is two
w plus three.

98
00:07:20,331 --> 00:07:26,735
Perimeter is two lengths plus two widths:
two times the quantity two w plus three,

99
00:07:26,735 --> 00:07:29,078
plus two w, equals fifty-four.

100
00:07:29,528 --> 00:07:36,199
That simplifies to six w plus six equals
fifty-four. So six w equals forty-eight,

101
00:07:36,199 --> 00:07:40,728
and w equals eight. The length is nineteen
centimeters.

102
00:07:40,866 --> 00:07:46,964
Your turn. Maya has a hundred twenty
dollars and saves fifteen dollars a week.

103
00:07:46,964 --> 00:07:51,800
Leo has sixty dollars and saves
twenty-five dollars a week. After how many

104
00:07:51,800 --> 00:07:54,218
weeks will they have the same amount?

105
00:07:54,668 --> 00:07:56,204
Pause the video and try it.

106
00:07:56,654 --> 00:08:02,919
Let w be the number of weeks. One twenty
plus fifteen w equals sixty plus

107
00:08:02,919 --> 00:08:04,121
twenty-five w.

108
00:08:04,571 --> 00:08:11,892
Subtract fifteen w and sixty from both
sides: sixty equals ten w. So w equals

109
00:08:11,892 --> 00:08:12,272
six.

110
00:08:12,722 --> 00:08:16,690
Check: after six weeks, each of them has
two hundred ten dollars.

111
00:08:17,833 --> 00:08:22,806
That completes Unit Two. Next, we'll start
Unit Three, solving and graphing

112
00:08:22,806 --> 00:08:27,978
inequalities. If this helped, subscribe to
School Math, Explained, and turn on

113
00:08:27,978 --> 00:08:31,294
notifications so you don't miss it. See
you there.

